
What is a List ?
--> List is an interface in Java Collection Framework that represents an ordered collection
    (sequence) of elements. Mutable - That means: you can change its contents after creation.
📦 Package: java.util

ListIterator → supports backward traversal
Iterator → forward only

🔹 Key Characteristics of List
✔️ Maintains insertion order
✔️ Allows duplicate elements
✔️ Index-based access
✔️ Allows multiple null values
✔️ Elements can be accessed, updated, removed by index

